WEBVTT

00:15:58.903 --> 00:16:03.399
it actually can be the motivation
that helps you make a much better talk.

00:16:03.423 --> 00:16:07.976
Like, use that to be the motivation
to keep working out there.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.370
And the fear will probably
get back under control.

00:16:11.394 --> 00:16:14.073
EG: Yeah, and it wouldn't hurt,
either, to be fully aware

00:16:14.097 --> 00:16:17.068
that the other 50 people speaking
at TED are equally terrified,

00:16:17.092 --> 00:16:18.710
whether they appear to be or not.

00:16:18.734 --> 00:16:21.695
And there's a shared humanity
in that experience of recognizing

00:16:21.719 --> 00:16:25.461
that everybody here thinks they're the one
who's not supposed to be here.

00:16:25.485 --> 00:16:28.862
CA: And another pillar, I think,
for you, that you talk about a lot

00:16:28.886 --> 00:16:31.203
is this idea of discipline, of showing up.